Well, finally there seems to be somebody with the same problem then I have
for more than a year: System clock stops, no response to keyboard anymore.
Login sometimes still works for a while, and a halt sometimes prevents to
mess up the harddrive. Reboot from another machine never worked in my
case.

I called Digital and they came and changed the mainboard, because they 
expected a hardware problem. But it did not help. 

I just figured out that something is wrong with my cron jobs. About every
hour root gets an email from the system:

From root  Sat Oct  2 16:01:01 1999
Date: Sat, 2 Oct 1999 16:01:01 +0200
From: root@ibt013.ibt.kfa-juelich.de (Cron Daemon)
To: root@ibt013.ibt.kfa-juelich.de
Subject: Cron <root@ibt013> run-parts /etc/cron.hourly
X-Cron-Env: <SHELL=/bin/bash>
X-Cron-Env: <PATH=/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin>
X-Cron-Env: <MAILTO=root>
X-Cron-Env: <HOME=/root>
X-Cron-Env: <LOGNAME=root>
X-Status: 
X-Keywords:
X-UID: 92

rdate: Connection refused


Strange enough, most of the time my system crashed exactely at this
time!!! So usually the times stoped one minute after the hour! 

So is it possible that there is a connection between the cronjob and
the halt of the system clock???

I really hope that there is a solution soon for this problem. Today I
had to crashes alreday.

P.S.: I'm running RH 5.2, but had the problem already with 5.0.

Jochen.





