With regards to your message at 06:15 PM 10/7/99 -0400, Izaak Bozof. Where 
you stated:


>Which is faster?  A DS-10 with a 21266 / 466 or an AlphaPC164LX with 21164 
>533?
>
>
>Compaq has got DS-10 on sale 
>(http://www.digital.com/alphaserver/ad/linux/index1.html) as a complete 
>system for $3K.  I can throw together an 164lx system similarly configured 
>for about 60% of that.
>
>izaak
The DS10 is about 60% faster at integer, and about 80% faster fp.
Unfortunately the DS10 is a small planar board in a desktop case, so the 
expansion is a bit limited.
Another "gotcha" on these is the mandatory IDE disk and the 128MB of RAM 
made up of 2 x 64MB SODIMMs.

