You didn't say what version of RedHat.

> Through experimentation and desperation I tried the following
> 'boot sda1:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda1'
> this resulted
> 
> Please wait while setting up devices...........
> Major devices are: fd (0002) sd (0008) sr (000B)
> MILO: Failed to load the kernel

In Alpha RedHat 6.0 and up, the kernel is in /boot/vmlinuz (just like
Intels).

boot sda1:boot/vmlinuz root=/dev/sda1

You can also boot once using the kernel floppy and look around to see
where the kernel is on the hard disk:

boot fd0:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda1

-- g


