Well, my 164LX still hangs sporadicly, though I'm not sure it's related to
the above problem.  My machine doesn't hang on boot, but randomly under load.
I have *no* further ideas about how to fix or debug the problem.  

Once again, here are the symptoms: Machine hangs.  I have had it totally lock
up, but I've also had it hang in an intermediate state where it is still
pingable.  Once console switching even worked, but not out of X.  It seems to
help if I build a non-modular kernel.  It still happens, but less frequently.
It also seems to be more frequent under X, but I've had it happen without X.
Same for the network - happens more frequently under heavy net traffic, but
still happens without the network configured.  It also seems less likely if I
boot from AlphaBIOS/Milo rater than SRM/aboot.  When it hangs from the console
(not X) I sometimes get dumped back into SRM.  It says "exit code 7.  Machine
check while in PALmode." (from memory).  I have played with examining the
registers, but see no clear pattern.

Hardware: 164LX2/533MHz.  Elsa GLoria Synergy 8MB (Permedia2).  4GB Segate
(ST34321A) IDE disk.  Built in CMD646 controller.  Booting through SRM/aboot.

I have tried moving my hard drive and video card to another identical machine
and had the same problems.  I've also tried using an S3 Virge Trio64 card with
the same behavior.  This seems to be independant of which kernel version I'm
running.  I've tried 2.0.36 and 2.2.[7-12].  Currently I'm running
